1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:03,500
Okay, so let's talk about the session.
好的，那我们来谈谈这个环节。

2
00:00:04,020 --> 00:00:11,230
It's my great pleasure to introduce Dr. Jim Fan, who is the director of robotics and the distinguished scientist at NVIDIA.
很荣幸向大家介绍英伟达机器人部门总监、杰出科学家范麟熙博士。

3
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:11,850
Take it away.
请开始吧。

4
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:12,540
Thank you.
谢谢。

5
00:00:21,890 --> 00:00:26,280
About two months ago was happy Thursday, September the 3rd.
大约两个月前，是令人开心的星期四，9月3日。

6
00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:31,590
The robots were partying, GPUs were spinning, life as a roboticist was good.
机器人在狂欢，GPU在运转，作为机器人研究者的生活很美好。

7
00:00:32,190 --> 00:00:34,120
And that's the day Astra dropped.
那一天，Astra发布了。

8
00:00:34,170 --> 00:00:40,180
I have never seen a paper in human history that shattered so many dreams.
我从未见过任何一篇论文，能如此彻底地击碎那么多梦想。

9
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:42,010
Yeah, I made it.
是的，我做到了。

10
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:44,040
I can hear the sound of your hearts breaking.
我能听到你们心碎的声音。

11
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:49,130
Then we did what any respectable scientific community would do.
然后，我们像任何有尊严的科学共同体一样做了事。

12
00:00:49,450 --> 00:00:51,950
We went through five stages of grief.
我们经历了五个悲伤阶段。

13
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:53,840
Denial.
否认。

14
00:00:54,380 --> 00:00:55,230
This is fake news.
这是假新闻。

15
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:56,140
These are cherry-picked.
这些都是挑出来的。

16
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:57,460
Anger.
愤怒。

17
00:00:57,720 --> 00:01:00,340
How dare they call themselves roboticists now?
他们居然还敢自称机器人专家？

18
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:01,390
Bargaining.
讨价还价。

19
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:03,300
They still need my motion planner, right?
他们还是需要我的运动规划器，对吧？

20
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:04,060
Right?
对吧？

21
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:08,940
Depression with a wine bottle, my PhD is now a joke in the system prompt.
抑郁，手里拿着一瓶酒，我的博士论文现在成了系统提示里的笑话。

22
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:12,800
And finally, acceptance, yeah, it's all over.
最后，接受了，是的，一切都结束了。

23
00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:18,540
Or as a friend summarized with dead eyes, winter is coming.
或者像一位朋友用无神的眼睛总结的那样：寒冬将至。

24
00:01:20,230 --> 00:01:27,510
Yet when we think that Astra is going to rule us all, this guy Diogo, he came along with Jeff, a new System 1 model.
然而当我们以为Astra将统治一切时，迪戈出现了，和杰夫一起带来了新的System 1模型。

25
00:01:27,790 --> 00:01:31,230
It's fast, reactive, and suddenly everyone's excited again.
它快速、响应灵敏，突然间所有人都再次兴奋起来。

26
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:38,870
So I argue that you can't possibly be excited about a System 1 for language models and hold a funeral for robotics,
所以我认为，你不可能对语言模型的系统1感到兴奋，同时又为机器人技术的消亡举行葬礼。

27
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:43,240
which needs to be faster, more reactive, and more local.
机器人技术需要更快、更灵敏、更本地化。

28
00:01:43,870 --> 00:01:48,670
So is System 1 still needed is the wrong question to begin with.
因此，系统1是否仍然必要，这个问题从一开始就错了。

29
00:01:49,470 --> 00:01:53,410
Because everything is going to be a skill, including System 1.
因为一切都会变成一种技能，包括系统1。

30
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:56,280
The right question is, what makes a good skill?
正确的问题是，什么样的技能才算好？

31
00:01:56,980 --> 00:02:02,220
Can you easily teach it by showing? can we easily steer it by reasoning?
你能通过演示轻松教会它吗？我们能否通过推理轻松引导它？

32
00:02:03,830 --> 00:02:05,490
And that's how we think about GR00T 2.
这正是我们思考 GR00T 2 的方式。

33
00:02:05,890 --> 00:02:09,950
From a full stack perspective, adaptable and steerable.
从全栈角度看，它具备可适应性和可引导性。

34
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:20,110
On a core model side of GR00T, it is a two billion parameter world action model that takes as input language, multi view, camera and state.
在 GR00T 的核心模型层面，它是一个拥有二十亿参数的世界动作模型，输入包括语言、多视角摄像头和状态信息。

35
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:24,680
And here, what you see, not a single pixel is real.
这里你看到的，没有一个像素是真实的。

36
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:27,280
You're watching the robot dreaming.
你正在观看机器人在做梦。

37
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:33,900
It's predicting the next few frames in the pixel space, and then acting upon that dream.
它在像素空间中预测接下来的几帧画面，然后据此采取行动。

38
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:40,900
And the model jointly decodes the action along with the predicted future frames in one diffusion pass.
该模型在一次扩散过程中联合解码动作和预测的未来画面。

39
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:46,480
We also designed GR00T 2 Turbo, optimized for efficient edge compute.
我们还设计了专为高效边缘计算优化的 GR00T 2 Turbo。

40
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:54,480
It uses four times fewer spatial video tokens, so it runs much faster while keeping the same two billion parameters.
它使用的空间视频词元数量仅为原来的四分之一，因此运行速度更快，同时保持了相同的二十亿参数。

41
00:02:55,690 --> 00:03:02,910
And we trained GR00T 2 on a huge corpus of well-annotated multi-view data that can be retargeted to the robot.
我们使用大量标注良好的多视角数据集对 GR00T 2 进行了训练，这些数据可被重新用于机器人。

42
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:06,320
So let's see GR00T 2 in action.
那么，让我们看看 GR00T 2 的实际表现。

43
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:11,120
This is the first clip, fully autonomous, no speed up and cut.
这是第一段视频，完全自主，无加速也无剪辑。

44
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:18,270
The robot carefully takes the memory stick out of GB300 and replaces it.
机器人小心翼翼地将内存条从 GB300 中取出并更换。

45
00:03:18,620 --> 00:03:22,520
So basically GR00T is maintaining the data center that is used to train GR00T.
本质上，GR00T 正在维护用于训练 GR00T 的数据中心。

46
00:03:23,330 --> 00:03:28,720
I hear that these days it's called recursive self-improvement, RSI.
我听说现在这被称为递归自我改进，简称 RSI。

47
00:03:28,770 --> 00:03:31,870
Maybe this is the first spark of physical RSI.
或许这正是物理 RSI 的首个火花。

48
00:03:33,490 --> 00:03:36,370
And here's a UPS store scenario.
这是一个 UPS 门店场景。

49
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:40,820
This demo is fine-tuned with only one hour of demonstration.
这个演示仅用一小时的示范数据进行了微调。

50
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:46,600
The robot picks up the scissors, it carefully wraps it around the fingers and it cuts the labels.
机器人拿起剪刀，小心地将其绕在手指上，然后剪下标签。

51
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:55,330
So some parts here, I have to speed up to fit the talk but I will keep the interesting bits at 1X real time.
所以这里有些部分我需要加快速度以适应演讲时间，但我将保持有趣的内容以1倍速实时播放。

52
00:03:55,380 --> 00:04:03,160
So, you can see it here, carefully peeling that label, this real time autonomous,
你看，它正在仔细剥离标签，这是实时的自主操作，

53
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:10,260
and then it will apply that label on the NVIDIA package, and it's gonna scan it.
然后它会将标签贴在英伟达的包装上，并进行扫描。

54
00:04:11,210 --> 00:04:15,490
And you can see that indicator whenever I speed up on the lower left corner.
你可以在左下角看到指示器，每当我在加快速度时它就会亮起。

55
00:04:17,010 --> 00:04:22,580
And here we take a page out of the high school chemistry lab, so this is crude salt filtering.
这里我们借鉴了高中化学实验室的做法，这是粗盐过滤实验。

56
00:04:23,060 --> 00:04:32,670
Basically the robot will scoop some salt into the beaker and it will start to dissolve it, and then it's gonna place that beaker onto that machine.
机器人基本上会舀一些盐放进烧杯，开始溶解，然后将烧杯放到那台机器上。

57
00:04:34,260 --> 00:04:38,560
So I have to speed this up because in GR00T 2, we're going all in on long horizon,
我必须加快这部分，因为在 GR00T 2 中，我们全力投入长程任务，

58
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:44,020
that's what manipulation, that pushes routinely beyond three minutes and even five minutes.
这类操作通常持续超过三分钟，甚至达到五分钟。

59
00:04:44,380 --> 00:04:51,880
That consists of 20 more steps, and every step has cascading error, so end-to-end is very difficult without a good model.
这包含了20个额外步骤，每个步骤都存在级联误差，因此没有一个良好的模型，端到端实现非常困难。

60
00:04:52,860 --> 00:04:59,000
And here is my favorite part, we teach the robot to clean up after itself, so we can spend less time resetting the scene.
这里是我最喜欢的部分，我们教机器人自己清理现场，这样我们就能节省更多时间来重置场景。

61
00:05:02,110 --> 00:05:10,550
And compared to baseline techniques, GR00T 2 and Turbo push the frontier into double digit gains over the prior state of the art.
与基线技术相比，GR00T 2 和 Turbo 将性能提升推向了超越以往技术水平的两位数增长。

62
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:19,880
A good System 1 skill must be easy to teach, so we introduce an emergent feature called X-Adapt.
一种优秀的 System 1 技能必须易于教授，因此我们引入了一种涌现能力，称为 X-Adapt。

63
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:21,900
And the idea is very simple.
核心理念非常简单。

64
00:05:22,420 --> 00:05:30,320
You collect data in an easy domain, like human wearables or simulation, and then you transfer those skills zero-shot onto the real robot.
你在人类可穿戴设备或仿真等简单领域收集数据，然后将这些技能零样本迁移到真实机器人上。

65
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:32,240
And let me give you some examples.
让我举几个例子。

66
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:38,500
This is a human wearing UMI grippers and collect the data on a long horizon assembly task.
这是一个人佩戴着 UMI 夹具，完成长程装配任务的数据采集。

67
00:05:39,270 --> 00:05:44,060
Then we fine tune GR00T 2 checkpoint on only the data from humans and zero
然后我们仅用人类数据对 GR00T 2 的检查点进行微调。

68
00:05:44,110 --> 00:05:48,930
shot transfer it to these yam grippers that actually look quite different from the UMI grippers.
将这个动作传输到这些夹爪上，它们实际上看起来与UMI夹爪差别很大。

69
00:05:49,470 --> 00:05:53,390
And the robot is able to complete this assembly task from end to end.
机器人能够从头到尾完成这项装配任务。

70
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:55,130
And this one is even harder.
而且这个更难。

71
00:05:55,180 --> 00:05:58,500
We captured the data in human mocap gloves.
我们通过人体动捕手套采集了数据。

72
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:06,310
So the part that you saw from crude salt filtering where the robot carefully places the filter and then it wets it
你看到的那段粗盐过滤过程，是机器人小心翼翼地放置滤纸，然后将其浸湿

73
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:16,060
and pour the salt water through that part can be entirely zero-shot adapted from the human mocap data with zero teleop.
将盐水倒入该部分，可完全通过零样本方式从人类动捕数据中适配，无需遥操作。

74
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:21,750
And with these devices, we can do these highly dynamic motions like tossing.
借助这些设备，我们可以完成抛掷等高度动态的动作。

75
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,280
That's very hard to teleop.
这非常难以通过遥操作实现。

76
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:27,640
And you can mix and match different types of robots on our warehouse line.
你可以在我们的仓库产线上随意搭配不同类型的机器人。

77
00:06:28,410 --> 00:06:31,080
And at our lab, we just have so many random stuff to throw.
在我们实验室里，堆满了各种乱七八糟的东西可以扔。

78
00:06:31,130 --> 00:06:33,490
So it's fun to see them just throwing stuff all day.
看它们整天扔东西，非常有趣。

79
00:06:35,420 --> 00:06:44,520
And to push X-Adapt even further, we designed these exoskeleton devices called DexUMI that has a one-to-one mechanical mapping to robot hands.
为了进一步推进 X-Adapt，我们设计了名为 DexUMI 的外骨骼设备，其机械结构与机器人手具有一对一映射关系。

80
00:06:45,660 --> 00:06:51,800
And we use those exoskeleton to collect the data and we fine-tune GR00T only on that data.
我们使用这些外骨骼采集数据，并仅用该数据对 GR00T 进行微调。

81
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:54,180
So this is fully autonomous.
因此这是完全自主的。

82
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:58,940
And yes, we do trust the robot with the knife.
是的，我们确实信任机器人使用刀具。

83
00:07:01,310 --> 00:07:08,170
And actually, after these experiments, our whole lab now smells like banana, because it's more than what we can humanly consume.
实际上，经过这些实验后，我们整个实验室现在都弥漫着香蕉味，因为产生的香蕉量远超人类能消耗的。

84
00:07:09,690 --> 00:07:14,290
So here the exoskeleton and the robot hand actually look very different from the video.
因此，视频中外骨骼和机器人手的外观实际上看起来与视频中大不相同。

85
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:20,420
So WAM's video pre-training helps bridge this visual gap zero-shot.
因此，WAM 的视频预训练有助于弥合这一视觉差距，实现零样本迁移。

86
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:22,220
And here comes my favorite.
然后就到了我最喜欢的环节。

87
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:24,920
You see how natural this twisting motion is?
你看这个扭转动作多么自然吗？

88
00:07:25,140 --> 00:07:27,780
You can't get that subtlety through teleop.
这种细微差别是遥操作无法实现的。

89
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:32,620
Because the mechanics of DexUMI is closely matched with the hand,
因为 DexUMI 的机械结构与人手高度匹配，

90
00:07:32,890 --> 00:07:38,150
we're able to capture these fine details of human dexterity directly onto the robot.
我们能够将人类灵巧性的细微特征直接捕捉并映射到机器人上。

91
00:07:39,980 --> 00:07:43,020
And then simulation is another very easy source of data.
然后，仿真也是数据的另一个非常容易获取的来源。

92
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:47,400
So we can train reinforcement learning in simulation, Isaac Lab,
我们可以在仿真环境中训练强化学习，使用 Isaac Lab，

93
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:56,210
and then we can generate synthetic data through domain randomization, and we fine-tune GR00T only on the same trajectories.
然后通过域随机化生成合成数据，并仅在相同轨迹上对 GR00T 进行微调。

94
00:07:56,260 --> 00:07:59,280
and with zero-shot X-Adapted into the real.
并通过零样本 X-Adapt 实现真实场景的部署。

95
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:03,920
So this part is real autonomous 1X, directly from the sim.
因此这一部分是真正的自主 1X，直接从仿真中生成。

96
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:08,260
And this also applies to whole body local manipulation.
这同样适用于全身局部操作。

97
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:14,500
This part is same in Isaac Lab, and this is zero-shot transferring to real at our kitchen.
这部分在 Isaac Lab 中是一样的，这是我们把零样本迁移应用到厨房真实场景中的例子。

98
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:23,820
And with X-Adapt, GR00T 2 Turbo paired with Sonic, the whole body controller that we introduced last year.
在 X-Adapt 的加持下，GR00T 2 Turbo 与我们去年推出的全身控制器 Sonic 配合工作。

99
00:08:24,940 --> 00:08:30,360
So here are our researchers drop coffee a lot at 2 a.m. when the human brains fail.
所以我们的研究人员经常在凌晨两点咖啡洒了一地，那时人类大脑已经撑不住了。

100
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:34,180
So we train our robot to clean up after us.
因此我们训练机器人来收拾我们的残局。

101
00:08:39,570 --> 00:08:41,210
After a while, it doesn't smell very good.
过了一段时间，味道就不太好了。

102
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:45,100
There's a whole basket of dirty towels.
整个篮子里都是脏毛巾。

103
00:08:46,940 --> 00:08:49,560
And then we also gave the robot a shift at Videsque Cafe.
然后我们还让机器人在 Videsque 咖啡馆轮班工作了一次。

104
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:53,760
Here's our researcher expressing approval of the robot's cleaning job.
这是我们的研究人员在肯定机器人打扫工作的表现。

105
00:08:54,660 --> 00:08:56,800
So the robot here is carrying two chips.
所以这里的机器人正拿着两个芯片。

106
00:08:57,320 --> 00:09:08,840
The GR00T 2 Turbo runs on the Jetson AGX Thor at 80 motion tokens a second, And Sonic runs on Jetson Orin and that's running at 50 Hertz whole body control.
GR00T 2 Turbo 在 Jetson AGX Thor 上以每秒 80 个动作 token 的速度运行，Sonic 则在 Jetson Orin 上运行，实现每秒 50 赫兹的全身控制。

107
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:14,500
So here is a party night at our lab and the robot serving popcorns.
这是我们实验室的派对之夜，机器人在分发爆米花。

108
00:09:16,510 --> 00:09:21,450
And actually we charge cash and we sell the popcorns.
实际上我们收现金，还卖爆米花。

109
00:09:21,830 --> 00:09:26,390
As far as I know, I think that's the only revenue that our team makes for the company.
据我所知，我认为这是我们团队为公司创造的唯一收入来源。

110
00:09:27,530 --> 00:09:30,600
So the ARR is about $20 per night.
所以每晚的年经常性收入约为20美元。

111
00:09:30,650 --> 00:09:35,440
Yeah, very diligent, working around the clock, selling popcorn.
是的，非常勤勉，全天候工作，卖爆米花。

112
00:09:38,910 --> 00:09:44,750
On our X-Adapt benchmark, GR00T 2 shows much stronger emergent transfer than baselines.
在我们的X-Adapt基准测试中，GR00T 2展现出比基线模型更强的涌现迁移能力。

113
00:09:46,180 --> 00:09:49,520
And next, GR00T 2 is more than a single model checkpoint.
接下来，GR00T 2远不止是一个单一模型检查点。

114
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:55,140
We blur the boundary of System 1 and 2 in what we call unified cognition.
我们在所谓的统一认知中模糊了系统1和系统2的界限。

115
00:09:56,330 --> 00:09:58,590
Here's an example instruction.
这是一个示例指令。

116
00:09:59,110 --> 00:10:02,860
You saw the trash by recycling and food waste and these complex criterion.
你看到了通过回收和食物垃圾以及这些复杂标准分类的垃圾。

117
00:10:02,910 --> 00:10:09,970
and Astra figures out the semantics of the scene and paints the guidance directly onto the pixels.
Astra 会理解场景的语义，并直接将引导信息绘制到像素上。

118
00:10:10,590 --> 00:10:12,990
So we call this new interface, WAM API.
因此我们称这种新接口为 WAM API。

119
00:10:14,070 --> 00:10:16,870
And GR00T 2 natively supports this type of visual steering.
GR00T 2 原生支持这种视觉引导类型。

120
00:10:17,330 --> 00:10:20,850
And in this way, we factor out reasoning from physics.
通过这种方式，我们将推理从物理中分离出来。

121
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:28,500
And with visual steering, Astra and GR00T 2 can go hand in hand to solve the Tower of Hanoi, Zero Shot.
通过视觉转向，Astra 和 GR00T 2 可以协同完成汉诺塔问题的零样本求解。

122
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:32,470
This is executing a physical recursion algorithm.
这是在执行一个物理递归算法。

123
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:38,480
You know, it will be completely unnecessary for a two billion model to be able to write a recursive code.
你知道，对于一个拥有二十亿参数的模型来说，能够编写递归代码完全是不必要的。

124
00:10:39,230 --> 00:10:47,130
So, WAM API allows GR00T 2 to offload cognition upstream and focus on what it does best.
因此，WAM API 使 GR00T 2 能够将认知任务上移，专注于它最擅长的部分。

125
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:52,040
And the whole system is able to recover from failure and verify success.
整个系统能够从故障中恢复并验证成功。

126
00:10:53,770 --> 00:10:56,510
Here's a second way to interface that we call WAM Edit.
这是第二种接口方式，我们称之为 WAM 编辑。

127
00:10:57,540 --> 00:11:04,820
So, Astra watches the camera feed, monitors the proprioception, and intervenes on the action execution directly.
Astra 会观察摄像头画面，监控本体感觉，并直接干预动作执行。

128
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:11,340
And GR00T 2 still handles the vast majority of the motion, and Astra only applies a delta when necessary.
GR00T 2 仍然负责绝大部分运动，Astra 只在必要时施加微调。

129
00:11:12,990 --> 00:11:15,110
And let me take you back to our chemistry lab.
让我带你们回到我们的化学实验室。

130
00:11:15,730 --> 00:11:17,910
Here's an end-to-end uncut scene.
这是一段端到端的完整未剪辑画面。

131
00:11:18,580 --> 00:11:24,480
The task is to take some substance here, put it on a tray, and watch it under the microscope.
任务是取一些物质，放到托盘上，然后在显微镜下观察。

132
00:11:25,220 --> 00:11:30,020
You know, for the System 1 model, sometimes it loses track of the repetitive motions,
对于 System 1 模型来说，有时会丢失对重复动作的追踪。

133
00:11:30,220 --> 00:11:38,500
and here Astra correctly intervenes on the proprioception and stops the dip at two dips specified by our system prompt.
这里，Astra 正确地干预了本体感觉，并在我们系统提示中指定的两个下垂处停止了动作。

134
00:11:39,650 --> 00:11:42,490
And then we also connect Astra to the microscope view.
然后我们还将 Astra 连接到显微镜视图。

135
00:11:43,470 --> 00:11:47,300
Then it's able to, here, here it comes.
然后它就能在这里，它来了。

136
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:50,860
It turns on the microscope, Astra is connected to the microscope,
它打开了显微镜，Astra 已连接到显微镜，

137
00:11:51,570 --> 00:12:00,400
and it instructs the robot hand to rotate just the right degree of angle so it comes in sharp focus.
并指示机械手旋转到恰好合适的角度，使图像清晰对焦。

138
00:12:00,450 --> 00:12:03,050
It's all real-time and cut autonomous.
全程实时且自主运行。

139
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:11,420
And the third way is through an agentic harness we developed in-house called Aspire that combines GR00T 2,
第三种方式是通过我们内部开发的代理式运行框架 Aspire，它结合了 GR00T 2，

140
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:15,580
native GR00T 2, with code-based skills authored by trial and error.
原生的 GR00T 2，以及通过试错编写出的代码技能。

141
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:24,060
And Aspire can switch seamlessly from GR00T 2 to code as policy for error recovery or monitor safety like a guardian angel.
Aspire 可以在 GR00T 2 和代码策略之间无缝切换，用于错误恢复或像守护天使一样监控安全。

142
00:12:25,500 --> 00:12:26,360
Here's how it works.
这就是它的运作方式。

143
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:30,650
We first construct a sim environment and have Astra explore with it.
我们首先构建一个仿真环境，并让 Astra 在其中探索。

144
00:12:30,700 --> 00:12:37,260
You can think of it as fine-tuning or priming Astra in code space without gradient descent.
你可以把它看作是在代码空间中对 Astra 进行微调或预训练，而无需梯度下降。

145
00:12:38,020 --> 00:12:38,960
So this is still insane.
所以这仍然令人难以置信。

146
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:42,740
And we can transfer this type of skills directly to the real world.
我们可以将这类技能直接迁移到现实世界中。

147
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:46,480
And GR00T 2 is part of the skill library.
GR00T 2 是技能库的一部分。

148
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:49,180
And here GR00T actually makes a mistake.
这里 GR00T 实际上犯了一个错误。

149
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:53,480
It got the upper side of the wing upside down.
它把机翼的上表面装反了。

150
00:12:54,020 --> 00:13:02,540
And Aspire executes a recovery poke that actually allows GR00T to resume control and install the upper wing correctly.
Aspire 执行了一次恢复性操作，实际上让 GR00T 恢复了控制，并正确安装了上机翼。

151
00:13:07,780 --> 00:13:14,660
And then we can just have a human dump the parts in any ways you want, and it just keeps assembling.
然后我们只需让人把零件随意丢进去，它就会持续组装下去。

152
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:18,420
It's so good that it basically turns reality into Minecraft.
它太厉害了，几乎把现实变成了我的世界。

153
00:13:20,350 --> 00:13:30,990
The robot just keeps working through the night and filling our Minecraft inventory day and night at essentially 100 % robustness.
机器人整夜不停工作，日以继夜地填充我们的我的世界库存，几乎实现了 100% 的鲁棒性。

154
00:13:32,930 --> 00:13:37,330
So being able to do this before 2027 is beyond my wildest imagination.
能在 2027 年之前做到这一点，已经超出了我最疯狂的想象。

155
00:13:37,990 --> 00:13:40,970
Neither Astra nor GR00T can do this alone.
Astra 和 GR00T 都无法单独完成这件事。

156
00:13:41,290 --> 00:13:42,290
And you need both.
你必须两者兼备。

157
00:13:44,030 --> 00:13:45,410
Remember these sad kittens?
还记得这些可怜的小猫吗？

158
00:13:46,340 --> 00:13:49,770
Turns out that we're one stage beyond celebration.
结果发现，我们已经超越了庆祝的阶段。

159
00:13:50,770 --> 00:13:56,590
Astra didn't shatter our dreams, but it shattered our walls.
Astra 没有击碎我们的梦想，却击碎了我们的壁垒。

160
00:13:57,370 --> 00:14:02,050
Frontier LLMs lower the barrier of entry and raise the ceiling for robotics.
前沿大模型降低了机器人技术的入门门槛，同时提升了其上限。

161
00:14:02,490 --> 00:14:09,930
And we as a community just have to admit that robotics is no longer an elitist sport anymore.
作为社区，我们必须承认，机器人技术已不再是精英专属的运动。

162
00:14:10,700 --> 00:14:14,200
The mission is too important to leave anybody out.
这项使命太重要了，不能让任何人掉队。

163
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:16,680
So GR00T is opening the gates.
所以 GR00T 正在打开大门。

164
00:14:17,770 --> 00:14:24,550
I'm excited to announce that both GR00T 2 and Turbo Weights and a X-Adapt recipe will be open source in December.
我很高兴宣布，GR00T 2 和 Turbo Weights 以及 X-Adapt 食谱都将在十二月开源。

165
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:27,420
You need to own System 1 untethered.
你需要拥有一个不受束缚的 System 1。

166
00:14:34,940 --> 00:14:41,380
You need to own System 1 untethered and free of the tyranny of conference wifi.
你需要拥有一个不受束缚的 System 1，摆脱会议场所 Wi-Fi 的束缚。

167
00:14:43,910 --> 00:14:45,430
And we're going more than that.
我们还将走得更远。

168
00:14:45,890 --> 00:14:47,710
We're open sourcing our simulation engine.
我们将开源我们的仿真引擎。

169
00:14:48,190 --> 00:14:52,510
This is Sim Foundry, our real-to-sim pipeline with physical validation.
这是 Sim Foundry，我们的真实世界到仿真环境的流程，并支持物理验证。

170
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:57,800
It supports features like particle physics, articulated objects, and so on.
它支持粒子物理、关节物体等特性。

171
00:14:58,530 --> 00:15:01,970
And with Astra, you can easily build sim at scale.
使用 Astra，你可以轻松实现大规模仿真构建。

172
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:07,740
Sim Foundry 1.0 is available today and 2.0 coming in early 2027.
Sim Foundry 1.0 今日可用，2.0 将于 2027 年初发布。

173
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:11,340
We're open sourcing our agentic harness.
我们将开源我们的代理式运行框架。

174
00:15:12,020 --> 00:15:13,010
This is Aspire,
这是 Aspire，

175
00:15:13,060 --> 00:15:21,860
our agent framework that learns a skill library that compounds over time and enables a new type of continual learning without gradient descent.
我们的智能体框架，能够持续学习技能库，随时间积累，并实现无需梯度下降的新一代持续学习。

176
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:25,020
We're open sourcing our annotation engine.
我们将开源我们的标注引擎。

177
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:30,680
This is Flora, our open model suite for massive scale data curation.
这是 Flora，我们用于大规模数据整理的开源模型套件。

178
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:36,340
It gives you these accurate curations, captions, auto evolves and reward functions.
它提供精准的数据整理、自动标注、自动演化和奖励函数。

179
00:15:36,980 --> 00:15:46,980
And if you host Flora locally, it's 125 times cheaper than Astra at the same performance We're open sourcing our training data.
如果你本地部署 Flora，其成本仅为 Astra 在同等性能下的 1/125。

180
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:54,500
This initiative called Human One Million is our high quality in-house training data.
这项计划名为“人类百万”，是我们高质量的内部训练数据。

181
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:59,020
And we are open sourcing the first 100,000 hours today.
而且今天我们正在开源前10万小时的训练数据。

182
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:04,160
And last but not least, we're even open sourcing our hardware design.
最后但同样重要的是，我们甚至会开源我们的硬件设计。

183
00:16:04,870 --> 00:16:11,120
So for all these devices you saw, the UMI, DexUMI, and the Flexible Neck, now you can build it in your own garage.
所以对于你们刚才看到的所有设备——UMI、DexUMI 和柔性颈部，现在你们可以在自家车库中自己动手搭建。

184
00:16:11,170 --> 00:16:12,760
We're giving you all the blueprints.
我们把所有设计蓝图都提供给你们。

185
00:16:12,810 --> 00:16:15,670
So it's really a leap of faith.
这真的是一次信念的飞跃。

186
00:16:15,850 --> 00:16:17,630
Take as much as you want.
想拿多少就拿多少。

187
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:28,830
We're building an open ecosystem and sending an open invitation because we would like people from all disciplines, all walks of life,
我们正在构建一个开放的生态系统，并发出开放的邀请，因为我们希望来自各个领域、各种背景的人们，

188
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:33,950
to build robots, to experience physical AGI firsthand,
都能来制造机器人，亲身体验物理 AGI，

189
00:16:34,290 --> 00:16:41,820
and to own a piece together in this greatest step function change that humanity has ever seen.
一起参与人类历史上最重大的跃迁式变革。

190
00:16:43,410 --> 00:16:49,430
And GR00T has brought to you, with so many sleepless nights and so much love from NVIDIA, Team Green.
GR00T 由英伟达绿色团队倾注无数不眠之夜与满满爱意，呈献给您。

191
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:52,160
And one more thing.
还有一件事。

192
00:16:53,470 --> 00:16:57,230
I'd like to show you a task that is impossible to teleop.
我想向你们展示一个无法通过遥操作完成的任务。

193
00:16:57,930 --> 00:17:01,230
That must be run at high inference rate locally.
这必须以高推理速率在本地运行。

194
00:17:02,330 --> 00:17:07,450
Autonomous, uncut, 1x speed, real time.
自主、未剪辑、1倍速、实时。

195
00:17:15,260 --> 00:17:17,370
And don't worry, we're good friends without fire marshal.
别担心，我们是无火警隐患的好朋友。

196
00:17:17,420 --> 00:17:21,840
That right there is the flame of hope.
那就是希望之火。

197
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:30,330
From now on, anyone could become a roboticist and everything that moves will be autonomous.
从现在起，任何人都可以成为机器人专家，所有移动的物体都将实现自主。

198
00:17:31,110 --> 00:17:33,850
And in that flame, summer is coming.
在那火焰之中，夏天即将到来。

199
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:35,040
Thanks.
谢谢。

200
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:39,300
Thank you, Jim.
谢谢你，吉姆。
